## Summary of Findings

The literature shows that online recruitment systems significantly improve the efficiency of hiring by automating job posting, application management, and candidate tracking. Existing platforms such as LinkedIn demonstrate the benefits of digital recruitment but may be expensive or overly complex for smaller organizations. The selected dataset provides realistic recruitment data that can be normalized and implemented in Oracle Database. Oracle PL/SQL offers the necessary programming features to automate recruitment processes, enforce business rules, and maintain data integrity.

---

## Research Gap

Many organizations, especially small and medium-sized enterprises, continue to rely on manual recruitment methods or expensive commercial platforms. There is a need for an affordable, secure, and database-driven recruitment system that demonstrates effective use of Oracle Database and PL/SQL while supporting applicant tracking and recruitment management.

---

## Conclusion

This research confirms that an Online Job Recruitment and Applicant Tracking System is a practical solution for improving recruitment processes. The findings support the design of an Oracle database capable of managing employers, applicants, job vacancies, applications, interviews, and recruitment reports through PL/SQL.
